Z||000000||mdjoneses||09-15-2000||06:02 AM||||Has anyone had any luck getting the ebrake recall done? I got the notice in 1991 and from what I can tell it was from that time forward. I need inspection sticker. Thanx  Mark/86/2.8se||||reg||2
Z||000001||fieroparts.com||09-15-2000||09:08 AM||||recalls are good forever, call 1800 pm cares or your local dealer to find out if you have any other open recalls on your car.<P>Hope to see you at the Fiero show on the 23rd<BR>in Rutland MA.<P>tim||||reg||10
Z||000002||whamel||09-15-2000||10:42 AM||||You have to go to the dealer now - 1800 PMCARES doesn't seem to have the Fiero listed as a vehicle anymore.<BR>  It's kinda sad really - a long time ago they got me a full set of docs and manuals for my 1966 bonneville for free so I could get it back to specs.  They used to be super helpful!  Last time when I got off the phone I was just mad about the whole conversation.||||reg||1
Z||000003||KevinP||09-15-2000||10:54 AM||||what exactly does the recall pertain to?  I can't even tell you how many problems I've had with my e-brake, so if I can have it recalled, that would be great.<BR>Thanks,<P>Kevin||||reg||5
Z||000004||theogre||09-15-2000||11:35 AM||||I don't think I have the full text on that one. I think it was actually for problems with the rear calipers more than just the E brake. Its a rebuild or replacement of the calipers themselves.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ROB MAC||09-15-2000||11:47 AM||||What my understanding was it replaced a part to make the ratcheting mechanism work properly. Ever notice that rear brakes pads don't seem to wear out? If you do not use your E-brake every once in a while they don't adjust. I had this recall done and a few weeks later I was doing brake work and I noticed the nut on the E-brake lever hadn't been touched in years. Totally rusted. NO wrench marks. E-brake still does not work properly. So I wonder how many of these recalls get done to spec.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mdjoneses||09-15-2000||02:11 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/86-c-16.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/86-c-16.htm</A>  This Fiero site has the details of the ebrake recall. My vin. is on the list but the dealer called someplace and said my car didn't need to be done. They said the recall notice I got was part of a mass mailing. If I can get my car going I'll try to hit Fiero gathering in Ma.  ||||reg||2
Z||000007||Monkeyman||09-15-2000||08:18 PM||||Someone correct me if I'm wrong but I don't think that <B>all</B> recalls are good forever.  Just the ones related to safety.  I don't know which category this would fit into (and don't really care since I don't have an E brake).||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||09-15-2000||08:32 PM||||There are 2 kinds of documents, recalls and TSB's.<P>Recalls are filled with and administered by <A HREF="http://www.nhtsa.gov/" TARGET=_blank>The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration (NHTSA)</A> and never expire. The engine fire campaign is such.<P>The others are manufacturor TSB's. They don't actually expire but they may cost you to get fixed. TSB's can cover anything. Sales notes about DexronIII, tighten this screw to stop roof rattle, how to fix TC lockup problems, etc.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||ka4nkf||09-15-2000||10:13 PM||||The recall was for straight shift only.<BR>not for auto tranny.||||reg||1
